-- חוק דמי מחלה, התשל"ו-1976 — sections 1, 2, 4, 4א, 5, 6 and 12: who is
-- an employee for the law and what an illness is, sick pay from the second
-- day of an absence for illness (half for the second and third, whole from
-- the fourth; from the first for a malignant illness's or dialysis's
-- treatments), a day and a half for each full month of work and no more
-- than 90, no dismissal of an employee absent for his illness while his
-- accrued days last, the wage it is paid on and its components, and that
-- the law takes no right a collective agreement gives. The text is
-- laws/sick-pay-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים הפתוח;
-- the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the takanon's §1.25.3.1, and the circulars and
-- agreements that follow it, rule on every subject of these sections
-- without citing the law. §1 leaves out of "an employee" one whose sick pay
-- a collective agreement regulates, which is every teacher here (the
-- takanon's sick leave is the 1.9.58 agreement's), so §§2 to 6 do not reach
-- a teacher; §4א does (its (ג)), and §12 keeps what the agreement gives.
-- Where an instrument rules on a subject of §§2 to 6, it is compared all
-- the same, so that no outcome turns on reading §1.
--
-- Time is counted as the law counts it: the absence and the accrual in
-- days, the work in months. A procedure the Minister sets by regulation
-- (§2(ג), §4(ד)) is not pinned; no rule here turns on one.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

§ `חוק דמי מחלה — הזכות, השיעור, הצבירה והגנה מפיטורים`

§§ `1`

-- "Employee": one whose payment for a period of illness is not regulated
-- by a collective agreement (an agreement, registered or not, another
-- collective arrangement, or an extension order). "Salaried": paid mainly
-- by the month or a longer period; "wage-earner", every other. "Illness":
-- the temporary or permanent inability to do his work that follows, on
-- medical findings, from ill health.
@ref law:1
GIVEN `a collective agreement regulates his payment for a period of illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employee as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` `a collective agreement regulates his payment for a period of illness` IF
    NOT `a collective agreement regulates his payment for a period of illness`

@ref law:1
GIVEN `unable, for a time or for good, to do his work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it follows, on medical findings, from ill health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an illness as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` `unable, for a time or for good, to do his work` `it follows, on medical findings, from ill health` IF
    `unable, for a time or for good, to do his work` AND `it follows, on medical findings, from ill health`

@ref law:1
`the Sick Pay Law's words for an illness` MEANS "אי כשרו הזמני או הקבוע של העובד לבצע עבודתו, הנובע, על פי ממצאים רפואיים, ממצב בריאות לקוי"

#ASSERT `an employee as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `an employee as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `an illness as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` TRUE FALSE

§§ `2`

-- (א): an employee absent from work because of illness is paid by his
-- employer, within the maximum of §4: (1) from the fourth day of the
-- absence, sick pay; (2) for the second and third, half of it; the first,
-- nothing, unless the Minister's regulations say otherwise. (א1): one who
-- had a malignant illness, or an illness that needs regular dialysis, and
-- is absent for its periodic treatment or tests, after recovery too, is
-- paid from the first day, or part of it, on a doctor's written
-- confirmation. (ב)(1): a salaried employee's period of illness is every
-- day of it, weekly rest and holidays included; (2)–(5): a wage-earner's
-- leaves them out, in proportion for one who did not work full time.
-- (ג): procedures and the date of payment are the Minister's regulations.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for its first day
      `treatment or tests of a malignant illness or dialysis, on a doctor's confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of sick pay section 2 gives for the day` `day of the absence` `treatment or tests of a malignant illness or dialysis, on a doctor's confirmation` IS
    BRANCH IF `treatment or tests of a malignant illness or dialysis, on a doctor's confirmation` THEN 1
           IF `day of the absence` AT LEAST 4 THEN 1
           IF `day of the absence` AT LEAST 2 THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 2
           OTHERWISE 0

-- The days of sick pay section 2 gives for an absence of so many days,
-- counting from its first: what an instrument that pays every day is
-- compared with.
@ref law:2
GIVEN `days of the absence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of sick pay section 2 gives for an absence of` `days of the absence` IS
    IF `days of the absence` AT MOST 1
    THEN 0
    ELSE `half days` PLUS `whole days`
    WHERE
        `half days`  MEANS (min 2 (`days of the absence` MINUS 1)) DIVIDED BY 2
        `whole days` MEANS max 0 (`days of the absence` MINUS 3)

@ref law:2
`section 2(ב)(1) counts a salaried employee's weekly rest and holidays in his period of illness` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `the share of sick pay section 2 gives for the day` 1 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the share of sick pay section 2 gives for the day` 3 FALSE EQUALS 1 DIVIDED BY 2
#ASSERT `the share of sick pay section 2 gives for the day` 4 FALSE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the share of sick pay section 2 gives for the day` 1 TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `days of sick pay section 2 gives for an absence of` 1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `days of sick pay section 2 gives for an absence of` 3 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `days of sick pay section 2 gives for an absence of` 10 EQUALS 8

§§ `4`

-- (א): the period of sick pay is no more than a day and a half for each
-- full month worked for the employer or at the workplace since the law
-- applied to him, and no more than 90 days, less the days already paid
-- under the law. (ב): a month in which he did not work every working day
-- counts as full at 25 working days (21⅔ in a five-day week), and part of
-- one gives a proportional share. (ג): a period insured under §§8 and 9
-- is not counted. (ד): the Minister may regulate the method.
@ref law:4
`days of sick pay a full month of work accrues under section 4` MEANS 3 DIVIDED BY 2

@ref law:4
`most days of sick pay section 4 lets accrue` MEANS 90

@ref law:4
GIVEN `full months worked for the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `days of sick pay already paid under the law` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of sick pay section 4 leaves him` `full months worked for the employer` `days of sick pay already paid under the law` IS
    max 0 (`the days accrued` MINUS `days of sick pay already paid under the law`)
    WHERE
        `the days accrued` MEANS
            min `most days of sick pay section 4 lets accrue` (`full months worked for the employer` TIMES `days of sick pay a full month of work accrues under section 4`)

@ref law:4
GIVEN `working days he worked in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the workplace works a five-day week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of a full month section 4(ב) counts` `working days he worked in the month` `the workplace works a five-day week` IS
    min 1 (`working days he worked in the month` DIVIDED BY `a full month's working days`)
    WHERE
        `a full month's working days` MEANS
            IF `the workplace works a five-day week` THEN 65 DIVIDED BY 3 ELSE 25

-- A year of full months: 18 days.
`days of sick pay a year of work accrues under section 4` MEANS
    12 TIMES `days of sick pay a full month of work accrues under section 4`

#ASSERT `days of sick pay a year of work accrues under section 4` EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `days of sick pay section 4 leaves him` 100 0 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `days of sick pay section 4 leaves him` 10 3 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the share of a full month section 4(ב) counts` 13 FALSE EQUALS 13 DIVIDED BY 25

§§ `4א`

-- (א): an employer does not dismiss an employee absent for his illness in
-- the period of sick pay accrued to him under the law or under a
-- collective agreement, up to the maximum of §4. (ב): not where (1) the
-- employer gave notice of dismissal under the Prior Notice Law before the
-- absence began, or (2) the workplace stopped for good, or the employer is
-- bankrupt or (a body) wound up. (ג): here "employee" includes one whose
-- sick pay a collective agreement regulates — so this section, unlike §§2
-- to 6, reaches a teacher.
@desc What the Sick Pay Law forbids an employer.
DECLARE `Sick Pay Law act` IS ONE OF
    `dismiss an employee absent for his illness while his accrued sick-pay days last`

@ref law:4א
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Sick Pay Law act`
DECIDE `no dismissal in the accrued sick-pay days` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `dismiss an employee absent for his illness while his accrued sick-pay days last`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Sick Pay Law, section 4א: an employer does not dismiss an employee absent for his illness in his accrued sick-pay period"

-- The days of an absence §4א protects: those accrued to him, under the law
-- or a collective agreement, but no more than §4's maximum for the months
-- he worked.
@ref law:4א
GIVEN `sick-pay days accrued to him, under the law or a collective agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `full months worked for the employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of an absence section 4א protects` `sick-pay days accrued to him, under the law or a collective agreement` `full months worked for the employer` IS
    min `sick-pay days accrued to him, under the law or a collective agreement`
        (`days of sick pay section 4 leaves him` `full months worked for the employer` 0)

@ref law:4א
GIVEN `absent for his illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of the absence before the dismissal` IS A NUMBER
      `sick-pay days accrued to him, under the law or a collective agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `full months worked for the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `notice of dismissal given before the absence began` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the workplace stopped for good, or the employer is bankrupt or wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4א bars the dismissal` `absent for his illness` `days of the absence before the dismissal` `sick-pay days accrued to him, under the law or a collective agreement` `full months worked for the employer` `notice of dismissal given before the absence began` `the workplace stopped for good, or the employer is bankrupt or wound up` IF
        `absent for his illness`
    AND `days of the absence before the dismissal` LESS THAN `the days it protects`
    AND NOT `notice of dismissal given before the absence began`
    AND NOT `the workplace stopped for good, or the employer is bankrupt or wound up`
    WHERE
        `the days it protects` MEANS
            `days of an absence section 4א protects` `sick-pay days accrued to him, under the law or a collective agreement` `full months worked for the employer`

@ref law:4א
`section 4א reaches an employee whose sick pay a collective agreement regulates` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `days of an absence section 4א protects` 300 240 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `days of an absence section 4א protects` 40 240 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `section 4א bars the dismissal` TRUE 60 100 240 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 4א bars the dismissal` TRUE 90 100 240 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 4א bars the dismissal` TRUE 10 100 240 TRUE FALSE

§§ `5`

-- (א): sick pay is the wage he would have been entitled to in the period
-- had he gone on working; (ב): one paid by output, at his average output of
-- the three months before.
@ref law:5
GIVEN `the wage he would have had working` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick pay section 5 gives` `the wage he would have had working` IS
    `the wage he would have had working`

#ASSERT `sick pay section 5 gives` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `6`

-- (א): the wage sick pay is calculated on counts the basic wage, the
-- seniority supplement, the cost-of-living supplement, the family
-- supplement and a departmental or professional supplement. (ב): a wage
-- not paid by these components counts the day's ordinary wage with any of
-- them paid. (ג): the Minister may set another method by regulation.
@desc A component of the wage section 6(א) counts for sick pay.
DECLARE `wage component section 6 counts` IS ONE OF
    `the basic wage`
    `the seniority supplement`
    `the cost-of-living supplement`
    `the family supplement`
    `a departmental or professional supplement`

@ref law:6
`the wage components section 6 counts` MEANS
    LIST `the basic wage`, `the seniority supplement`, `the cost-of-living supplement`, `the family supplement`, `a departmental or professional supplement`

#ASSERT count `the wage components section 6 counts` EQUALS 5

§§ `12`

-- (א): an employee entitled to sick pay both under the law and under the
-- terms agreed or customary at his work has it under the one he chooses —
-- for a right measured in one number, the larger. (ב): the law takes away
-- no right a collective agreement gives, whether the law applies to the
-- employees or not.
@ref law:12
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the agreed terms give` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 12 of the Sick Pay Law` `what the law gives` `what the agreed terms give` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the agreed terms give`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 12 of the Sick Pay Law` 18 30 EQUALS 30
